+-# AnonSync slim C++ working cube — rev0658
++# AnonSync slim C++ working cube — rev0659
+ 
+ AnonSync is a **C++ peer-to-peer file synchronization system**. The product target is Resilio Sync-style local folder replication across authorized devices: discover peers, compare authenticated file manifests, transfer missing content-addressed chunks, apply creates/updates/deletes exactly once, preserve conflicts honestly, and resume after interruption without a central service being the ordinary source of truth.
+ 
+-The current C++ cube does not yet implement the whole sync product. It contains a security and durability substrate that a sync engine needs, plus the sync-domain model seam started in rev0651, tightened at folder-manifest level in rev0652, connected to live local folder scans in rev0653, extended in rev0654 with deterministic local/remote manifest diff planning, advanced in rev0655 with local apply planning, advanced in rev0656 with verified staged-file materialization, tightened in rev0657 with stale-target overwrite preflight, and now extended in rev0658 with safe remote tombstone application. Existing authorization/replay/effect machinery remains subordinate to concrete sync mutations such as `publish_manifest`, `reserve_chunk_transfer`, `commit_file_version`, `apply_tombstone`, and `record_conflict`.
++The current C++ cube does not yet implement the whole sync product. It contains a security and durability substrate that a sync engine needs, plus the sync-domain model seam started in rev0651, tightened at folder-manifest level in rev0652, connected to live local folder scans in rev0653, extended in rev0654 with deterministic local/remote manifest diff planning, advanced in rev0655 with local apply planning, advanced in rev0656 with verified staged-file materialization, tightened in rev0657 with stale-target overwrite preflight, extended in rev0658 with safe remote tombstone application, and now extended in rev0659 with conflict-copy preservation for regular local files. Existing authorization/replay/effect machinery remains subordinate to concrete sync mutations such as `publish_manifest`, `reserve_chunk_transfer`, `commit_file_version`, `apply_tombstone`, and `record_conflict`.
+ 
+-Rev0658 keeps the code in C++ and fixes the next unfinished local mutation: `DeleteLocalPath` was only an intent. A Resilio-style sync system must apply deletes as carefully as it applies file bytes. Rev0658 adds `apply_sync_remote_tombstone`, validates that the apply entry came from `ApplyRemoteTombstone`/`DeleteLocalPath`, rebinds the remote tombstone digest/version evidence, rejects staging/conflict paths, preflights the current target against the planned local file evidence, removes only regular files, and emits `sync-tombstone:v1:` commit evidence.
++Rev0659 keeps the code in C++ and fixes the next unfinished local mutation: `PreserveConflictCopy` was only an intent. A Resilio-style sync system must not silently overwrite one side of a concurrent edit. Rev0659 adds `apply_sync_conflict_preservation`, validates that the apply entry came from `RecordConflict`/`PreserveConflictCopy`, rebinds remote entry digest/version evidence, preflights the current local file against the planned manifest evidence, copies that local file to a deterministic conflict path, verifies staged remote file bytes when the remote side is a file, and then either promotes the remote file or applies the conflicting remote tombstone. It also fixes an apply-plan validator bug that incorrectly required a remote staging path for file/delete conflicts.
+ 
+ ## Active sync mission
+ 
+@@ -17,20 +17,22 @@
+ 5. commit file mutations idempotently and crash-safely;
+ 6. preserve enough local evidence to distinguish synced, pending, conflicted, deleted, failed, and unknown states after restart or restore.
+ 
+-## Rev0658 changes
++## Rev0659 changes
+ 
+-- Adds `SyncTombstoneApplicationOptions` and `SyncTombstoneApplicationResult` to the public C++ sync-domain API.
+-- Adds `apply_sync_remote_tombstone` for executing `DeleteLocalPath` apply-plan entries produced from `ApplyRemoteTombstone` diff-plan actions.
+-- Adds `sync-tombstone:v1:` idempotency evidence bound to the remote tombstone entry digest, publisher-neutral remote version digest, local apply intent key, path, and absolute target path.
+-- Reuses the rev0657 stale-target discipline for deletes: a planned local-file delete requires the current target size and SHA-256 to still match the manifest evidence; a remote-only tombstone requires the target to remain absent.
+-- Rejects symlink ancestors, symlink targets, directories, non-regular files, appeared targets, disappeared planned targets, and changed planned targets before deletion.
+-- Extends `--selftest-sync-domain-model` to cover successful tombstone deletion, already-absent tombstone no-op, stale changed target rejection, and target-appeared rejection.
+-- Adds rev0658 docs, audit record, source patch, validator, build/test logs, active binary, and package manifest.
++- Adds `SyncConflictPreservationOptions` and `SyncConflictPreservationResult` to the public C++ sync-domain API.
++- Adds `apply_sync_conflict_preservation` for executing `PreserveConflictCopy` apply-plan entries produced from `RecordConflict` diff-plan actions.
++- Adds `sync-conflict:v1:` idempotency evidence bound to remote entry digest/version evidence, the local apply intent key, target path, staging path, conflict-copy path, and local entry/version evidence.
++- Fixes the local apply-plan shape validator so file/delete conflicts do not falsely require a staged remote file.
++- Preserves the planned local regular file by copying it to the deterministic conflict-copy path only after the current target still matches the planned local size and SHA-256.
++- For file/file conflicts, verifies the staged remote file against manifest chunk/content hashes, rechecks the local target after copying, then promotes the remote file to the original target path.
++- For file/delete conflicts, copies the local file to the conflict path, rechecks the local target after copying, then removes the original target to reflect the conflicting remote tombstone.
++- Extends `--selftest-sync-domain-model` to cover file/file conflict preservation, stale local conflict rejection before copy, and file/delete conflict preservation.
++- Adds rev0659 docs, audit record, source patch, validator, build/test logs, active binary, and package manifest.
