+ ## Honest ceiling
+ 
+-AnonSync is the product. The current package is still a local C++ library/CLI and deterministic harness. It is **not yet** a production peer discovery system, LAN/WAN/NAT traversal layer, encrypted peer protocol, file watcher, persistent manifest database, chunk transfer engine, conflict-copy materializer, mobile/desktop daemon, or privacy-preserving distributed sync deployment. Rev0658 can scan live local files into manifests, plan local/remote reconciliation, turn that reconciliation into local filesystem intents, materialize a fully staged remote file after verification, reject stale local target overwrites, and execute remote tombstones against regular files after stale-target preflight. The next code-bearing revision should add chunk receipt/write accounting or conflict-copy materialization.
++AnonSync is the product. The current package is still a local C++ library/CLI and deterministic harness. It is **not yet** a production peer discovery system, LAN/WAN/NAT traversal layer, encrypted peer protocol, file watcher, persistent manifest database, chunk transfer engine, partial-transfer/resume engine, mobile/desktop daemon, or privacy-preserving distributed sync deployment. Rev0659 can scan live local files into manifests, plan local/remote reconciliation, turn that reconciliation into local filesystem intents, materialize a fully staged remote file after verification, reject stale local target overwrites, execute remote tombstones against regular files after stale-target preflight, and preserve regular local files as conflict copies before applying a conflicting remote file or tombstone. The next code-bearing revision should add chunk receipt/write accounting or persisted manifest/index state.
